commit 15ec54b589d1e99bcc132a086cbcf1ceb31b4073
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 28 08:47:37 2026 +1100

    l3: Lock ItemAllocator and write its state atomically
    
    The fip link-local and rule-priority allocators are shared by every
    router on the agent but had no lock, and _write truncated and rewrote
    the state file, so concurrent workers could corrupt what the next
    restart reads. Lock each allocator and replace its file atomically.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    Change-Id: I33c5ac70b219fd82cfd8f0f6a2d7c1a41d2650a1
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

